ready: 1
kind: rule
id: agents.rule.settings-merge
display_id: RULE-AGENTS-SETTINGS-MERGE
module: agents
title: Changing a runtime's configuration safely
summary: Kernle adds or removes only its own entries, keeps everything else exactly, and can always be undone.
constraints:
  - text: Hook and server lists are merged by appending Kernle's entries; existing entries keep their order and content.
    hard: true
  - text: An entry already present is not added twice.
    hard: true
  - text: A configuration file that does not parse is refused with nothing changed and the parse error shown.
    hard: true
  - text: Before any change the file is copied to a timestamped backup beside it, and the new content is written to a temporary file and renamed into place.
    hard: true
  - text: Removal deletes only entries that carry Kernle's command or plugin name and leaves every other entry as it is.
    hard: true
when: Setup or removal changes a runtime's configuration file
then: The rule's constraints apply to every write of that file
